<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an algorithm to compute <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{e}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{e}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> in time <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{O(vc^{4})}\cdot n^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{O(vc^{4})}\cdot n^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of a minimum vertex cover of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the order of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first describe the algorithm and then prove its correctness and time-complexity.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> be the given graph. Also, let <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{u_{1},\dots,u_{vc}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{u_{1},\dots,u_{vc}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a minimum vertex cover of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=V\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=V\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math> be an independent set. We partition <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. For every vertex <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{I}(u)\leq 5vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{I}(u)\leq 5vc</annotation></semantics></math>, we include all the vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{I}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{I}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.Once we have finished considering all the vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, we place the remaining vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}=G[C\cup I_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}=G[C\cup I_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}=G[C\cup I_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}=G[C\cup I_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> (see <a href="#S3.F2" title="In 3.2 Vertex cover number ‣ 3 FPT algorithms ‣ Graph Irregularity via Edge Deletions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). We will show later that this results in <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I_{1}|\leq 5vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{1}|\leq 5vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V(G_{1})|\leq 5vc^{2}+vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V(G_{1})|\leq 5vc^{2}+vc</annotation></semantics></math>. We can now guess the projection <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of an optimal edge-irregulator <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=S\cap E(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=S\cap E(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}-S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}-S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not necessarily locally irregular. All that remains to do is to compute the smallest set <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}\subseteq E(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}\subseteq E(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G-(S_{1}\cup S_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G-(S_{1}\cup S_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is locally irregular. Notice that such a set <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contains only edges between the vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote these edges.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Henceforth, we focus on <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[vc]=\{1,\dots,vc\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[vc]=\{1,\dots,vc\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define a <span id="Thmproofx4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">modifier</span> <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. These modifiers encode the number of edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that need to be removed in order to arrive to a locally irregular graph. That is, if <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> incident to <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are removed from <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is not in conflict with any of its neighbours (in <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>). Note that for each <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the modifier <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> does not necessarily have a unique value. We will nevertheless show that it is sufficient to compute a minimum (with respect to summation) tuple <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{1},\dots,k_{vc})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{1},\dots,k_{vc})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i=1}^{vc}k_{i}\leq vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i=1}^{vc}k_{i}\leq vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproofx4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correctness.</span> We first argue about the size of <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_numclaim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 3.5</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I_{1}|\leq 5vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{1}|\leq 5vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproofx4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of the claim.</span>
Consider how <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed. By definition of <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, every vertex of <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> adjacent to a vertex of <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has degree at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5vc</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|I_{1}|=|\{N[v]|v\in C,d(v)\leq 5vc\}|\leq 5vc\cdot|C|=5vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>v</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{1}|=|\{N[v]|v\in C,d(v)\leq 5vc\}|\leq 5vc\cdot|C|=5vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamond" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋄</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamond</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_numclaim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 3.6</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}\subset E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}\subset E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of edges. For any optimal edge-irregulator <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> coinciding with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cap E_{2}\leq vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cap E_{2}\leq vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproofx4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of the claim.</span>
Let <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal edge-irregulator of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> coinciding with <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume by contradiction that <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cap E_{2}&gt;vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cap E_{2}&gt;vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since all the edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has one endpoint in <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, by the pigeonhole principle, there exists a vertex <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> adjacent to at least <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc+1</annotation></semantics></math> edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. If at least <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2vc+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2vc+1</annotation></semantics></math> edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent to <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, then we first remove <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc</annotation></semantics></math> of them from <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> may not yet be an edge-irregulator but the only conflicts we may have created are between <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and other vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> (since all the other neighbours of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are not in <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and thus have degree at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc</annotation></semantics></math>). Either way, since the other vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> can forbid at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc-1</annotation></semantics></math> conflicts, there exist a number <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq vc</annotation></semantics></math> such that increasing the degree of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> removes all these conflicts. Since there are at least <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc+1</annotation></semantics></math> vertices of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cap E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cap E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that are still adjacent to <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we can remove <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> of them to solve all the conflicts. This leads to a smaller edge-irregulator <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\cap E_{1}=S\cap E_{1}=S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\cap E_{1}=S\cap E_{1}=S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a contradiction to the optimality of <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamond" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋄</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamond</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_numclaim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 3.7</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal edge-irregulator of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v_{1},v_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v_{1},v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be three vertices with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2}\in I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2}\in I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv_{1}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv_{1}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv_{2}\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv_{2}\in E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv_{2}\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv_{2}\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists an optimal edge-irregulator <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=(S\setminus\{uv_{1}\})\cup\{uv_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=(S\setminus\{uv_{1}\})\cup\{uv_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproofx4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of the claim.</span>
First, note that the proof of Claim <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Claim 3.6 ‣ Proof ‣ 3.2 Vertex cover number ‣ 3 FPT algorithms ‣ Graph Irregularity via Edge Deletions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> also proves that if <math id="Thmproofx4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal edge-irregulator of <math id="Thmproofx4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, for any vertex <math id="Thmproofx4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C</annotation></semantics></math> which has neighbours in <math id="Thmproofx4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproofx4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G-S}(u)&gt;vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G-S}(u)&gt;vc</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Consider now <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=(S\setminus\{uv_{1}\})\cup\{uv_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=(S\setminus\{uv_{1}\})\cup\{uv_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}=G-S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}=G-S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2}\in I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2}\in I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, their degrees are at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc</annotation></semantics></math> and all their neighbours have a degree of at least <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> does not create any conflicts for <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> or for <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, all the other vertices in <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> have the same degree and the same neighbourhood in <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G-S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G-S</annotation></semantics></math> and in <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G-S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G-S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, since <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> was an edge-irregulator, they are not in conflict with each other. Thus, <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is an edge-irregulator.
 <math id="Thmproofx4.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diamond" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋄</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diamond</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproofx4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Running time.</span> By Claim <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Claim 3.5 ‣ Proof ‣ 3.2 Vertex cover number ‣ 3 FPT algorithms ‣ Graph Irregularity via Edge Deletions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, we have that <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C\cup I_{1}|\leq vc+5vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C\cup I_{1}|\leq vc+5vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, there are at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{(vc+5vc^{2})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{(vc+5vc^{2})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> possible guesses of <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Claim <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Claim 3.6 ‣ Proof ‣ 3.2 Vertex cover number ‣ 3 FPT algorithms ‣ Graph Irregularity via Edge Deletions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>, we know that an optimal edge-irregulator of <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> has at most <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{2}|\leq vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{2}|\leq vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to Claim <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Claim 3.7 ‣ Proof ‣ 3.2 Vertex cover number ‣ 3 FPT algorithms ‣ Graph Irregularity via Edge Deletions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>, it suffices to guess for each vertex <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C</annotation></semantics></math> how many edges of <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> incident to <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> are in <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, a tuple of integers <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{1},\dots,k_{vc})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{1},\dots,k_{vc})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}+\dots+k_{vc}\leq vc^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}+\dots+k_{vc}\leq vc^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="vc^{vc^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">vc^{vc^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> such possibilities. Recall that checking whether a set <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset E(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset E(G)</annotation></semantics></math> is an edge-irregulator can be done in running time <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the order of <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, and since we repeat this step for each guess of <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the running time of this algorithm is <math id="Thmproofx4.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{(vc+5vc^{2})^{2}}\cdot vc^{vc^{2}}\cdot n^{2}=2^{O(vc^{4})}\cdot n^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{(vc+5vc^{2})^{2}}\cdot vc^{vc^{2}}\cdot n^{2}=2^{O(vc^{4})}\cdot n^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
